{"h":2857,"lines":[{"w":0.071773376464843719,"x":0.83961712024418567,"y":0.050227066655937347,"t":"Reading","h":0.021734955762965913,"c":1},{"w":0.64359863281249996,"h":0.017570019769368228,"t":"which are located anywhere trom 15 to 100 kilometres trom the major hill site.","c":1,"x":0.23010379769285672,"y":0.10174418576464783},{"t":"Containing stone residences and walls, they likely belonged to local chiefs who","w":0.65051905314127612,"c":1,"y":0.11918604654008003,"x":0.23010379514050575,"h":0.019022491113383833},{"h":0.020391178598263782,"c":1,"t":"acted as servants to the king.","y":0.13535359379028955,"w":0.24614257812500001,"x":0.22818896353236701},{"x":0.22145328754928092,"h":0.01761273957366627,"t":"The Mapungubwe plateau has a very high number of carnivore animal remains","y":0.17424772581956871,"c":1,"w":0.65397923787434897},{"x":0.23005048759267746,"w":0.63159484863281257,"y":0.19175183566084775,"t":"and ivory splinters, suggesting that the skins of these large animals and ivory","h":0.020484592632616705,"c":1},{"t":"elephant tusks were accumulated, probably for trade with coastal areas reached","y":0.21063680890822589,"h":0.019014353848905152,"c":1,"w":0.65743942260742183,"x":0.23010381802247365},{"t":"by the Limpopo River. The presence of glass beads, almost certainly from India,","c":1,"h":0.017561883172261483,"x":0.22837370849286004,"y":0.22953114036052158,"w":0.6557093302408854},{"y":0.24447308132055956,"x":0.22823698406108983,"c":1,"w":0.66811747233072905,"h":0.02158413574026552,"t":"indicate there was trade of some sort with other states on the coast who, in turn,"},{"x":0.22837369767528229,"h":0.017510009028846474,"y":0.26592022380629454,"c":1,"w":0.66782007853190106,"t":"traded with merchants travelling from India by sea. Mapungubwe also benefitted"},{"w":0.66955017089843749,"h":0.017511026103484872,"x":0.22837370339183566,"y":0.28481455556896962,"t":"from locally-sourced copper and the gold trade as it passed from the kingdom of","c":1},{"t":"Great Zimbabwe (12-15th century), situated to the north of Mapungubwe, to the","h":0.021979193824250176,"w":0.66455459594726562,"c":1,"x":0.22999751626304657,"y":0.29983530128807523},{"w":0.66782007853190106,"x":0.22837369767909668,"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1,"t":"coastal city of Kosala. It is likely that trade links led to a strengthening of political","y":0.32120363901450588},{"x":0.22837371104982329,"y":0.33866279072578087,"w":0.64878890991210936,"h":0.018929931314947579,"c":1,"t":"authority in order to control and even monopolise these lucrative interregional"},{"h":0.013761421614714275,"w":0.10756448109944661,"y":0.35845781386892628,"x":0.23005477092697457,"t":"connections.","c":1},{"h":0.017581208257761993,"c":1,"y":0.39389534900719281,"x":0.22664360554387883,"w":0.63321797688802084,"t":"Archaeological discoveries reveal that pottery was produced on a scale large"},{"x":0.22831242122032697,"h":0.020761352389571219,"y":0.41108011030172076,"w":0.66448191324869788,"c":1,"t":"enough to suggest the presence of professional potters, and is another indicator"},{"y":0.4297598729820189,"w":0.6627289326985677,"c":1,"h":0.020640377901583129,"x":0.22832244330106183,"t":"of the prosperity of Mapungubwe society. Archaeological finds include spherical"},{"y":0.4491279070027594,"t":"vessels with short necks, beakers, and bowls, many of which have decorative","x":0.22837369900737475,"w":0.62975779215494798,"c":1,"h":0.019031645452500801},{"x":0.22837371043630772,"h":0.019030627710490577,"c":1,"w":0.63321797688802084,"t":"stamps. There are also ceramic discs, and whistles. In addition, cattle, sheep,","y":0.46802325584185522},{"w":0.64013839721679688,"x":0.2283737078362382,"h":0.019056055911192971,"y":0.48530440893785376,"c":1,"t":"and goat figurines, and small figures of highly stylised humans with elongated"},{"w":0.62802769978841144,"y":0.50419874062171566,"t":"bodies and short limbs have been found. The figures may have been used in","x":0.22837369329640902,"c":1,"h":0.017603585234549302},{"c":1,"t":"ceremonies as offerings to ancestors, but their precise function is not known.","x":0.22828500538733409,"w":0.63509653727213544,"y":0.52049372880088762,"h":0.02317016953934814},{"y":0.54058782370684066,"w":0.67474049886067711,"c":1,"h":0.019005199509788184,"t":"Other discoveries include small jewellery items made from locally sourced copper.","x":0.22837369512878317},{"w":0.58996541341145825,"x":0.21453286418934511,"h":0.018953325366373175,"t":"Beautifully decorated artefacts made of gold have also been found at","y":0.57697690715516836,"c":1},{"t":"Mapungubwe. A type of decoration, tound nowhere else except Great Zimbabwe,","x":0.23183392243978573,"y":0.59727081904709833,"w":0.67301035563151046,"h":0.016101273896395485,"c":1},{"w":0.68001836140950522,"y":0.6133514122284458,"c":1,"t":"involved the crafting of gold into small rectangular sheets and carving geometrical","x":0.22660955464985325,"h":0.020328035881837958},{"t":"patterns into it. These sheets were then used to cover wooden objects (which","x":0.22837370217700281,"h":0.017494751574527623,"y":0.63226032205576299,"c":1,"w":0.63840830485026057},{"c":1,"h":0.020348837861153823,"w":0.63840830485026046,"x":0.22664359833751063,"t":"have not survived) using small tacks, also made of gold. One such object that","y":0.64970930199637356},{"y":0.66790591153140555,"w":0.66794250488281248,"h":0.022299665767383958,"c":1,"t":"has been discovered may have been a sceptre, while additional evidence of local","x":0.22659696540092417},{"t":"gold-working is a rhinoceros figurine made from small hammered sheets, and","y":0.68660592873577342,"c":1,"x":0.22833330718437111,"w":0.6367566935221356,"h":0.019895296650720318},{"y":0.70639534855359032,"w":0.64878890991210936,"t":"thousands of small gold beads. These objects were all found at the royal burial","x":0.22664360721923441,"h":0.017537471378825442,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.72529069739230256,"t":"site and date to c. 1150. They are the first known indicators that gold had an","x":0.2266436009102597,"h":0.017536454304187155,"w":0.63148788452148441},{"y":0.74273255785527048,"t":"intrinsic value of its own (as opposed to that of a currency) in southern Africa.","w":0.64013839721679699,"h":0.017589345522240563,"c":1,"x":0.22491350034090365},{"y":0.77906976723670918,"t":"The kingdom of Mapungubwe was already in decline by the late 13th century,","x":0.22318339351960106,"h":0.019040799791617657,"w":0.64705881754557293,"c":1},{"x":0.22837369967333832,"c":1,"w":0.6453287251790365,"h":0.017441861023846261,"y":0.79796511599369035,"t":"probably because overpopulation placed too much stress on local resources, a"},{"x":0.22664360979624443,"y":0.81686046483427932,"t":"situation that may have been brought to a crisis point by a series of droughts.","w":0.64186848958333331,"c":1,"h":0.01744186102384615},{"h":0.018756615523277564,"c":1,"y":0.83427553213512551,"t":"Trade routes may also have shifted northwards. Certainly, the areas that now","w":0.63157669067382816,"x":0.22659690688821665},{"w":0.45501729329427087,"c":1,"t":"prospered were to the north, such as Great Zimbabwe.","y":0.85304408683130128,"x":0.22664360241260964,"h":0.019048936388724513},{"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477,"y":0.95348837179415158,"t":"4З","w":0.022491348584492976,"x":0.88408304534443161}],"w":2400}